# Exhaustiveness checking for bare NominalVariant scrutinee (Task 11).
# A single-constructor type declaration produces a bare NominalVariant (not wrapped in Union).
# Coverage checking must use ConstructorSignature::from_nominal_variant (not from_union).
# The wildcard arm covers all constructors — no non-exhaustive error should be raised.
[
  Tag: [type [MyTag value: Int]]

  extract: [fn [let s@Tag]
    [match s
      _: 0
    ]
  ]

  result: 42
]
=== out
Dict({"MyTag": Function(payload), "extract": Function(s), "result": Int(42)})
